Architecture plan for mike-t-302f-test-website-005 issues #23-#27

Product and app shape
- Product name: mike-t-302f-test-website-005.
- Current stack: Vite + React + TypeScript single-page landing page.
- Product copy and labels should continue to come from PRODUCT.md and src/content/siteContent.ts.
- CTA destinations should continue to come from src/config/env.ts via VITE_CTA_URL.

Module structure and file organization
- src/App.tsx: compose the full landing page and pass the resolved CTA URL into sections/layout.
- src/content/siteContent.ts: add footer CTA content, footer link groups, and any test-facing section metadata.
- src/types/content.ts: extend SiteContent with footer CTA/link contracts and keep section IDs typed for nav and tests.
- src/components/layout/Footer.tsx: evolve from simple copyright/nav into the footer CTA section for issue #23.
- src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx and Header.tsx: keep semantic landmarks and anchor navigation centralized.
- src/components/sections/: keep page sections data-driven and expose stable IDs for a11y and E2E coverage.
- src/components/ui/: keep Button, Section, Card, and AccordionItem as shared primitives; add only small testable primitives if repetition appears.
- src/config/env.ts: remain the single place that validates VITE_CTA_URL.
- tests/unit or src/**/*.test.tsx: Vitest + React Testing Library component/content tests for issue #25.
- tests/e2e/: Playwright landing page tests for issue #26.
- README.md and .env.example: run, build, preview, deploy, and environment documentation for issue #27.

Dependencies between issues
- #23 should be implemented first among this set because it completes the visible page surface and expands footer content/types.
- #24 depends on all visual sections, including #23, so the responsive and accessibility pass should happen after the footer CTA lands.
- #25 depends on completed component/content behavior; tests should cover the footer CTA, section rendering, UI primitives, and VITE_CTA_URL wiring.
- #26 depends on a stable rendered page and test tooling from #25; Playwright should verify load, section presence, anchor scrolling, and CTA hrefs.
- #27 should be last because production build/deploy prep should document the final scripts, env requirements, static dist output, and verification path.

Key design decisions
- Keep the landing page static and client-rendered; no router or state library is needed.
- Keep CTA links as real anchors using the normalized URL from getAppEnv so header, hero, and footer behavior stays consistent.
- Use semantic landmarks: header, main, footer, section headings, nav labels, and real buttons/links.
- Preserve visible focus states and WCAG AA contrast while using existing Tailwind CSS theme tokens in src/index.css.
- Prefer data-testid only where role/name queries are brittle; tests should primarily assert accessible roles, names, headings, and links.
- Playwright should run against the Vite dev server or preview server and set VITE_CTA_URL to a deterministic test URL.
- Production deploy prep should treat dist/ as generated output, keep secrets out of git, and document static hosting requirements rather than committing build artifacts.
